    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How does Gemini 3.7 Flash compare to GPT-5.6 Luna and Claude?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "At $0.75/$3.75 per 1M, Gemini 3.7 Flash undercuts GPT-5.6 Luna (which OpenAI cut roughly 80% on July 30, 2026) on output and sits at a fraction of an Opus-class flagship's cost. Media reporting (VentureBeat, MarkTechPost, Times of India) framed the launch as a coding-and-agents push with a 50% introductory price cut. A provider review gateway like FreeModel lets you compare live per-workload costs across both in one dashboard." }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What can developers build with Gemini 3.7 Flash on the API?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Google targets it at complex coding, agentic workflows, and reliable multi-step execution. That makes it a fit for AI coding assistants, agent orchestration, tool-use loops, RAG-heavy copilots, and any high-volume task that previously needed a more expensive model. Like other Gemini Flash tiers it supports the same generateContent and streaming endpoints, with thinking tokens counted in output pricing." }
